<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toulouse</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Toulouse is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. As Tolosa it was the chief town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volcae">Volcae</a> Tectosages and then a Roman city; it was the capital of the Visigothic kingdom from 418 to 507 and later of the counts of Toulouse, rulers of much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/languedoc">Languedoc</a>, until the Albigensian Crusade brought it under the French crown in 1271. It is now a centre of the aerospace industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toulouse.jpg" alt="Toulouse" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frédéric Neupont · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Toulouse_-_vue_du_Vieux_Toulouse_depuis_St_Sernin_06.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
